<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamid II of Pontianak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1913–1978</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Hamid II, Syarif Hamid II Alkadrie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamid II was the last reigning sultan of Pontianak in West Kalimantan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, from 1945. He led West Kalimantan within the federal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Indonesia, served as a minister of state and led the design of the national emblem, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garuda-pancasila">Garuda Pancasila</a>. In 1950 he was arrested over links to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-westerling">Raymond Westerling</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance">APRA</a> coup attempt and imprisoned until 1958.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamid-ii-of-pontianak.jpg" alt="Hamid II of Pontianak" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Syarif_Hamid_II_of_Pontianak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
